proof.text:
The closed-stratum sheaf $i^*E=F|_Z$ is locally constant of finite type; the one-stratum argument, which was proved for every scheme, gives $i^*E\cong
u_Z^*H$ for an étale module sheaf $H$. The immersion $i$ is qcqs: on an affine open $\operatorname{Spec}A\subset W$ its inverse image is the affine $\operatorname{Spec}(A/I)$ by [lem-weil-pbc-reduced-induced-closed-subscheme], hence quasi-compact by [lem-weil-pbc-affine-scheme-qcqs]; For quasi-separatedness, clause (a) of [lem-weil-pbc-closed-immersion-integral-separated-uc] says that $i$ is separated, so its diagonal is a closed immersion. Clause (b) of the same node says that this diagonal is affine. Its inverse image over an affine open is therefore affine and hence quasi-compact by [lem-weil-pbc-affine-scheme-qcqs]; thus the diagonal is quasi-compact and $i$ is quasi-separated. Apply [sk-thm-pe-direct-image-comparison] to $H$ placed in degree zero to get $
u_W^*Ri_{\Et,*}H\cong Ri_{\Proet,*}
u_Z^*H$. Taking degree-zero cohomology gives $
u_W^*i_{\Et,*}H\cong i_{\Proet,*}
u_Z^*H$: comparison inverse image is exact by [det-pe-classical-sheaves-modules], and for any left exact direct image $i_*$ and an injective resolution $0	o H	o I^0	o I^1	o\cdots$, the kernel of $i_*I^0	o i_*I^1$ is $i_*H$. Thus $i_*i^*E$ is classical. This degree-zero argument does not require exactness of the étale closed direct image.
